\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
At Gaussian SK $\beta =1$, does the Gibbs probability of initial states whose continuous-time total-variation distance exceeds 1/4 at any deterministic $t_n=o(n^{2/3})$ tend to one in disorder probability? Ask for the same claim at $k_n=o(n^{5/3})$ single-site discrete updates.

